#   ==== H4. safety games on cyclic graphs ====
#   A NODE is Scott data `node bad successors`, a boolean and a list of
#   nodes. `safe n` answers false when every path from n reaches a bad node
#   or a node with no successor, trying the successors left to right, and
#   has no head when some path from n goes on forever through good nodes:
#   it never answers true. By Koenig's lemma it answers `false`
#   exactly when all paths are finite, so its absence of a head is the
#   greatest fixed point, `nu X. not bad and some successor in X`, the
#   CTL property EG good.
